      "writtenOn": "2024-03-21T14:31:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e If a salt has been recorded, shouldn\u0027t we always use it in this \"legacy\" mode?\n\nI dont follow, the salt field is obsolete when `llpvm_changes` is `false`  \u0026 can be anything (in this particular implementation, it will be exactly equal to salt_from_instance_id()). Is this the leagcy mode you are referring to?\n\n\n\u003e In particular as we\u0027re telling the guest that new_instance\u003dfalse?\n\nThe new-instance is unrelated to salt. It is used to ensure host can\u0027t inject empty Microdroid partition into instance.img while keeping the valid non-empty pvmfw partition, fooling Microdroid into booting different payloads \u0026 leaking secrets. [When the expectation is do-not-defer-rbp]\n\n\n\u003e llpvm_changes flags covers both implementing Sk, and switching to use instance ID\n\nYes, that is true. To elaborate on this:\n\nllpvm_changes \u003d true \u003d\u003e salt is obsolte, but Secretkeeper may or may not be present.\n\nSecretkeeper present \u0026\u0026 llpvm_changes is false \u003d\u003e Hopefully should never happen, possibly untested path\n\nSecretkeeper absent \u0026\u0026 llpvm_changes is false \u003d\u003e Pre Q3 Android, insatance.img is used with salt, code hashes \u0026 everything",
      "parentUuid": "2a133d9e_70a413d5",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 167,
        "startChar": 20,
        "endLine": 167,
        "endChar": 47
